   "confidence": "low",
   "notes": "28 Petty Cury (Boots, Lion Yard frontage, 1970s neo-Tudor ashlar). Ground floor is a recessed colonnade: square ashlar piers (pilasters) carrying the upper floors, with the dark-blue Boots shopfront set back behind them (recess not expressible in schema). Upper two floors: stone-mullioned rectangular windows, about two per bay. Bay count (6) and window x positions are estimated from oblique street-level views, not measured; pier spacing may differ. p0 is the east end (next to the arched timber door of the adjoining building)."
